1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,210
This clock runs slow.

2
00:00:02,250 --> 00:00:04,043
Nobody touched it.

3
00:00:04,083 --> 00:00:07,418
Its twin, outside, keeps perfect time.

4
00:00:07,458 --> 00:00:10,293
Broken? Or is time slower in there?

5
00:00:10,333 --> 00:00:12,310
Take it apart.

6
00:00:12,750 --> 00:00:16,210
Lift a clock about 1 foot. It runs faster.

7
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:19,171
Measured, with 2 atomic clocks.

8
00:00:20,292 --> 00:00:23,877
A couple of steps higher: you age faster.

9
00:00:23,917 --> 00:00:29,585
79 years: about 90 billionths of a second.

10
00:00:29,625 --> 00:00:31,627
Gravity slows time.

11
00:00:31,667 --> 00:00:34,726
Stronger gravity, slower clocks.

12
00:00:35,042 --> 00:00:38,210
LONGHOUR: what if you made the gravity?

13
00:00:38,250 --> 00:00:42,002
Sealed cabin. A dense ring spins round it.

14
00:00:42,042 --> 00:00:45,877
Spec: cabin clock −1 second a day.

15
00:00:45,917 --> 00:00:50,293
Trial 1: 24 h. Clock 1 second behind.

16
00:00:50,333 --> 00:00:54,585
Trial 2: ring at full speed. 1 h behind.

17
00:00:54,625 --> 00:00:57,085
Trial 3: a volunteer.

18
00:00:57,125 --> 00:01:01,225
1 day passes inside. Outside, a week.

19
00:01:01,333 --> 00:01:03,133
One catch.

20
00:01:03,208 --> 00:01:05,752
Inside, nothing feels slow.

21
00:01:05,792 --> 00:01:09,793
Watch, pulse, thoughts: all slow together.

22
00:01:09,833 --> 00:01:12,252
She gets no extra time.

23
00:01:12,292 --> 00:01:15,335
She just steps out into the future.

24
00:01:15,375 --> 00:01:17,437
There is no way back.

25
00:01:17,875 --> 00:01:19,793
LONGHOUR is cleared.

26
00:01:19,833 --> 00:01:22,853
As a one-way trip to the future.

27
00:01:23,083 --> 00:01:26,784
Next case Sunday. Follow @compandgrow.
